<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>@ViewData["Title"] - EF_learning</title>
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@6.0.0-alpha.1/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet" integrity="sha384-B/GM4XqrwHnWXNOWMbloTmrYXZg10cakYGmpfsR/bbzQ6JAJI4ihuyADKLnBgrCe" crossorigin="anonymous">
    <script type="module" src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@6.0.0-alpha.1/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js" integrity="sha384-1a/pXj49ZQ1aHEmrJ+gMw1otqoVsYwlEnlD8mIfY2TV03r20Y0CN7uqx1tQogjPL" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/lib/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/site.css" asp-append-version="true" />
   
</head>
<body>

    <mini-profiler />
    <div class="container">
        <main role="main" class="pb-3">
            @RenderBody() @*What is Rendered here is a specific view content, not the shared content*@
            
        </main>
    </div>

    @*Why I used the following three scripts ?

        Purpose: because I want to copy the server-side validation logic to the client.

        How will I  achieve that purpose ?
        Without jQuery Unobtrusive Validation, I would have to code the same validation logic in two places: once in the server-side validation attributes on model properties, and then again in client-side scripts
        Instead, I will use tag helpers in the view, tag helpers will use the validation attributes from the model properties to  generate data- attributes that will be parsed by the jQuery Unobtrusive Validation.

        the jQuery Unobtrusive Validation will send the validation logic to the jQuery.

    *@
    <script src="~/lib/jquery/dist/jquery.min.js"></script>
    <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jquery-validate/1.19.3/jquery.validate.js"></script> @*CDN*@
    <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jquery-validation-unobtrusive/3.2.12/jquery.validate.unobtrusive.js"></script>@*CDN*@
    
    <script src="~/lib/bootstrap/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script> @*needed for bootstrap to work*@
   
    @await RenderSectionAsync("Scripts", required: false)  @*This is needed because I defined sections inside the cshtml files*@
    @*
        For example, I have the following inside the Login.cshtml file:

        @section Scripts {
                <partial name="_ValidationScriptsPartial" />
            }

            so I should render the sections here, otherwise I will get error that says :
            An unhandled exception occurred while processing the request.
            InvalidOperationException: The following sections have been defined but have not been rendered by the page at '/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml': 'Scripts'. To ignore an unrendered section call IgnoreSection("sectionName").
    *@
    @await RenderSectionAsync("Styles", required: false)
    @await RenderSectionAsync("ImportFile", required: false)

    
</body>

</html>

